## Multiple organizations or regions

Provider configuration is per-organization, so managing more than one means one
aliased provider block per organization and a `provider` argument on each
resource.

## Inherited and effective values

A `upwind_threat_policy_rule` lives inside a `upwind_threat_policy`, and for the
nested object the Management API reports **effective** values - what applies
after inheritance - not what was written. Three fields behave this way:

| Field on the rule | Inherits from the policy when | Read back as                  |
| ----------------- | ----------------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| `severity`        | the rule sets no override     | the policy's `severity`       |
| `scope`           | the rule sets no override     | the policy's `resource_scope` |
| `is_enabled`      | the policy is disabled        | `false`                       |

For `severity` and `scope` the provider records only what the rule itself owns,
so an inherited value stays null in state and does not appear as drift on the
next plan. The read-only `scope_type` attribute names which side the effective
scope came from.

`is_enabled` is a ceiling rather than an override: a rule inside a policy with
`is_enabled = false` reads back as disabled whatever the rule asks for. To
enable a rule, enable its policy.

## Troubleshooting

Every API call the provider makes is logged. Set `TF_LOG=DEBUG` (or
`TF_LOG_PROVIDER=DEBUG` for provider lines only) and re-run the failing command:

```bash
TF_LOG=DEBUG terraform apply 2>&1 | tee tf.log
grep "Upwind API" tf.log
```

Each request logs the HTTP method and URL, the response status, its size, and how
long it took, alongside the Terraform operation it belongs to (`tf_rpc`) and the
resource or data source that triggered it. Credentials and request/response
bodies are never logged. The body of a *failed* call is not in the log but is in
the error Terraform prints, so include both when opening a support ticket - with
the `upwind_request_id` from the log line if one is present.

